Held fixed: the Part 0 utilities the cone calls (exact arithmetic): Mat.mulZ, Mat.pairZ, Mat.subZ, Mat.tabulate, eqZ, neZ, rank; with what they call: Mat.get, Mat.traceZ, Mat.transposeZ, rankAux.
In `main` but outside the readout (cannot change it): TwoPoint.valid, records, World.typeOf, World.wellFormed.
Types not mutated: World, TwoPoint, Assign, Formal, Rec.

Declared operators (each applied at every site the scanner finds in the 44 bodies):
  LIT      integer literal -> value - 1, value + 1
  NEG      delete a unary minus or Boolean not; sign of a negative literal
  LSW      swap two literals of one type and different value within one definition
  BLIT     Boolean literal true <-> false
  REL      negate a test (= / ≠, == / !=, eqZ, neZ, isSome / isNone); < -> ≤, ≥ and ≤ -> <, >
  QNT      list quantifier all <-> any
  LOG      && <-> ||, ∧ <-> ∨; drop the left or the right operand
  IF       swap the two branches of an if-then-else
  MATCH    swap the right-hand sides of two match arms
  AOR      binary + - * / % -> each of the other four; min <-> max
  VAR      one occurrence of a declared label -> its partner (end/role pairs, .1 <-> .2, readEnd <-> farEnd)
  ENDSWAP  every occurrence of one declared label pair in one definition exchanged
  LIST     list literal: drop or duplicate an entry
  CAT      ++ chain: drop or duplicate a summand
  CONS     :: chain: drop or duplicate an element
  label pairs (VAR, ENDSWAP): dA/dB, d1/d2, dc/df, i/j, a/b, s1/s2, i1/i2, c1/c3, f/g, xs/ys, odd/even, read1/read2, readEnd/farEnd, .1/.2 (a label is replaced only where its partner is in scope)
  pairs of mutations: every unordered pair whose sites are disjoint (a site is the token it rewrites, or the whole if / match / list / chain / connective node it moves or drops)

Single mutants: 818 = 166 LIT + 12 NEG + 93 LSW + 4 BLIT + 58 REL + 7 QNT + 36 LOG + 33 IF + 7 MATCH + 125 AOR + 180 VAR + 45 ENDSWAP + 22 LIST + 22 CAT + 8 CONS
  predicted to fail to elaborate: 47 (7 match arm uses a variable of the other pattern, 14 negative Nat literal, 26 projection swap on Int x Assign); by operator: LIT 14, MATCH 7, VAR 19, ENDSWAP 7
Pairs: 334153 unordered pairs, 331490 with disjoint sites; 37105 of these contain a mutant that fails to elaborate; 294385 are evaluated.
Space: 818 + 331490 = 332308 mutants.

== 2. Validation of the Python transcription (chainalpha_transcription.py) ==
  hooks named in the transcription (with its tables INT_LITS, HETERO_PROJ) = sites of the generator other than MATCH: True (418 sites; the 7 MATCH sites need no hook: every match swap moves a pattern variable out of its arm and fails to elaborate)
  unmutated readout: ([(1, 79), (2, 48), (3, 42), (6, 3)], 31104); the statement of `dressing_of_the_qutrit_qubit_link`: ([(1, 79), (2, 48), (3, 42), (6, 3)], 31104); equal: True
  upstream_mutations_lean.out (Lean 4.35.0 on the author's 19 rewordings + BASE): 20 of 20 lines reproduced character for character (main / commutators verdicts and readout)
  reads_at_qubit is the pair readEnd:IF:0=swap & farEnd:IF:0=swap
  X_at_far_end is the single mutant wX:VAR:0=farEnd
  exch_shift1 is the single mutant exch:LIT:0=1
  drop_fixed is the single mutant recs:CAT:0=drop2
  drop_even is the single mutant recs:CAT:0=drop1
  The other 14 rewordings change several tokens or add code; they are not single or paired mutants.
  Lean itself on the generated mutants: proofs/lean/chain-theory/mutation_spotcheck.sh -> mutation_spotcheck.out (all singles and a seeded sample of pairs).

